import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(CheckoutService.class);

log.info("User {} logged in", userId);   // level + timestamp + class, filterable
log.debug("cart={}", cart);              // suppressed in prod, string not even built
```

Parameterized `{}` means when DEBUG is off, `cart.toString()` is never called — a real performance win on hot paths.

```java
public OrderResult checkout(CheckoutRequest req) {
    // Boundary in: WHO and WHAT, never card data
    log.info("Checkout start: userId={}, items={}", req.userId(), req.itemCount());
    try {
        OrderResult r = process(req);
        log.info("Checkout ok: orderId={}, total={}", r.orderId(), r.total()); // business event
        return r;
    } catch (PaymentDeclinedException e) {
        log.info("Checkout declined: userId={}, reason={}", req.userId(), e.code()); // expected
        throw e;
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Checkout failed: userId={}", req.userId(), e); // failure + stack trace
        throw e;
    }
}
// NEVER: log.info("card={}", req.cardNumber());  <-- secret leak
```

