// With logstash-logback-encoder, log as key-value via the SLF4J fluent API / MDC
import net.logstash.logback.argument.StructuredArguments;

log.info("order_placed",
    StructuredArguments.kv("userId", userId),
    StructuredArguments.kv("orderId", orderId),
    StructuredArguments.kv("total", total));
// Output: {"message":"order_placed","userId":7,"orderId":42,"total":99.99}
// Now: total > 50 is a simple field query in Kibana/Datadog.
```

```java
// Structured JSON + a correlation ID is what makes aggregation powerful
MDC.put("requestId", requestId);
log.info("order_placed orderId={} total={}", orderId, total);
// Shipped as JSON, indexed by requestId/orderId, queryable across all instances:
//   requestId:"abc-123"  -> every line for this request, on any box
```

The app's only job is to emit good structured logs; the shipper, store, and UI handle the rest.

```java
import org.slf4j.MDC;
import java.util.UUID;

public class RequestIdFilter implements Filter {
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest req, ServletResponse res, FilterChain chain)
            throws IOException, ServletException {
        MDC.put("requestId", UUID.randomUUID().toString()); // set once per request
        try {
            chain.doFilter(req, res); // every log line downstream now carries requestId
        } finally {
            MDC.clear(); // CRITICAL: clear so pooled threads don't leak the value
        }
    }
}
```

